"Davrar was once governed by a council of eighty-nine seats, each with an equal vote."
"Changing the Mandate of Davrar needed a council vote unanimous but for one."
"The council of eighty-nine was dissolved when its veto system broke; Conclaves replaced it."
"Council members are sworn to vote as the Conclave wills; Davrar implements its will."
"Mortality was built into Davrar's founding; no council can change it."
"Questors listen only to those known across Davrar for deeds; a Conclave needs such backing."
"A Conclave opens with a speech by whoever called it, who may cede it to another."
"The opening speech cannot be challenged, has no time limit, and sets what is discussed."
"Any attendee may petition to speak; Davrar grants the stage alternating between sides."
"Davrar sets the speaking queue from all Questors' desires, putting the audience first."
"General speeches get five minutes before a challenge window; under a minute is best."
"After a speech, attendees may bid to challenge the speaker to a duel to the death."
"A speaker faces at most three challenges per speech; Davrar picks those with most merit."
"Davrar picks the challengers it judges most likely to beat the speaker."
"Davrar cuts no one off; it simply sends the challengers when time is up."
"A speaker must survive the challenges to speak again; winning all lets them reclaim the stage."
"A challenge winner may give a few words, a single refutation; duels are no free speaking slot."
"A duelist may speak next only if they petitioned for the slot."
"Exhibition matches may be offered but need not be accepted; there are no team duels."
"A losing challenger, like a slain speaker, is exiled from the Conclave and its continent."
"A Questor slain in a Conclave duel is exiled from the continent while the Conclave lasts."
"If a side loses all its speakers, the other side holds the stage until the vote."
"It is frowned upon to speak twice in a row or linger onstage."
"No fighting is allowed but agreed duels, and Davrar enforces this."
"Davrar teleports speakers and duelists to the stage."
"The stage reshapes between a podium and a sealed duel bubble."
"Davrar keeps mental and social skills from acting on the audience; they still guide the speaker."
"Davrar suppresses interference in duels and damps the voice of anyone speaking out of turn."
"Anyone may ask Davrar to verify a statement; it answers literally, without nuance."
"Davrar checks each proposal; an unworkable policy cannot be voted on."
"Davrar can validate a proposal conditionally, pending detailed guidelines."
"Once a proposal is validated, votes may be called and every Questor may vote."
"A measure passes only with a majority of all Questors; abstaining counts as no."
"Questors vote through interface notifications within seconds; most watch from afar."
"The vote-caller sees yes, no and abstain bars in their vision."
"Non-binding polls and binding final votes both exist."
"Every Questor is granted access to the continent where a Conclave meets."
"Politicking mostly happens before a Conclave, in private meetings."
"The Kalis Conclave ended in a catastrophic war."
"Sarya once forced a Conclave that failed."
"Years later the Heirs won the right to call a Conclave by winning a Polite War."
"That Conclave met at the Arena of the Concord in Dawn's Concord, with record attendance."
"Hundreds of thousands of Questors attended; every mortal speech there left deaths."
"Years later the Continuance Charter passed there; its first poll ran 2% above the threshold."
"Only 3% abstained in the first Charter poll, unusually few."
"Nathan's antimagic made Davrar's teleport to the stage fail without visible effect."
"Davrar sent no notification when Nathan secretly breached the arena."
